cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this unit in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "verifiedmethods unit A2: iterative methods for linear systems"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tiamiyu
    given-names: "Abd'gafar Tunde"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1641-7196"
    affiliation: "School of Mathematics, Jilin University"
version: "0.1.0.dev0"
license:
  - BSD-3-Clause
  - CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://verifiedmethods.github.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/verifiedmethods/linear-systems"
abstract: >-
  An open, verification-first teaching unit on stationary iterative methods for
  linear systems (Jacobi, Gauss-Seidel, SOR). Students write one sweep of each
  method and verify it against the theory: the observed convergence factor must
  match the spectral radius of the iteration matrix. An automatic check produces
  a verification report for their supervisor.
keywords:
  - numerical analysis
  - linear systems
  - iterative methods
  - verification
  - research methods
  - Nigeria
